.TH SLKTEST 1 "2026-10-16" "SparkLink development" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slktest \- SparkLink application channel correctness and load tests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slktest --adapter
.I ADAPTER
.B channel
.I ping|rate|window|duplex|peer CONNECTION
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses ordinary delegated channel file descriptors. slctl and slkd manage devices,
connections and authorization. This tool is not a Host or protocol Engine.
Capture, kernel selftests, formal verification and qualification aggregation
remain independent facilities. Experimental drivers and WS73 tests are VM-only.
.SH MODES
ping initiates one-outstanding-request measurement. peer replies to ping, or to
rate/window with --load. rate uses absolute --interval-us schedules. window
bounds outstanding application requests with --window. duplex runs on both ends
and independently sends, validates and replies. Measurements require a new
--report file. Application windows are not protocol credit.
.PP
--check on ping/peer runs existing correctness receipts instead of measurement.
It permits 1..20 --count and 29..2042 --bytes. --exercise selects regular,
boundaries, prefix-close or burst. Prefix-close is initiator1x2042; burst is
initiator16x2042. Peers use regular. Dynamic correctness requires --source-port,
--destination-port and --aid together; --hold retains the fd until a close line.
Dynamic measurement is not supported.
.SH BOUNDS AND FAILURE
Measure count is 1..10000, bytes29..2042 within actual basic CUTC MTU/MPS.
Rate/window/duplex and peer --load wait at most30s for start followed by newline.
Message original deadlines, finite queues, random validation, error and timeout
records remain enforced. Reports never grant performance qualification.
See channel subcommand --help and the versioned documentation for precise bounds.
.SH STATUS
Basic CUTC measurements and limited dynamic correctness only. Reliable modes,
protected security and safe TCID reuse are not promised. New executable names
never requalify historical artifacts. Full Native/WS73 and performance gates
must be run against the exact new binary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the selected exercise/measurement completed locally; it is not RF
qualification. Invalid input, timeout, correctness or resource failures are
nonzero. Incomplete reports and stderr must be retained.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slctl (1),
.BR slkd (8)
